                    <value>High</value>
                </Data>
                <Data name="Discussion">
                    <value>1. South of the Gulf of Tehuantepec: An area of low pressure is expected to form within the next day or  two to the south of the Gulf of Tehuantepec.  Afterward,  environmental conditions appear favorable for gradual development,  and a tropical depression is expected to form late this weekend or  early next week while the system moves slowly west-northwestward to  northwestward, parallel to the coast of southern and southwestern  Mexico. 
 Formation chance through 48 hours...medium...40 percent. 
 Formation chance through 7 days...high...90 percent. </value>
                </Data>
            </ExtendedData>
